```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant User
  participant Frontend
  participant API
  participant DB
  participant Worker
  participant XAPI

  User->>Frontend: create post (draft)
  Frontend->>API: POST /posts (save draft)
  API->>DB: insert POST (status=DRAFT)
  User->>Frontend: schedule post
  Frontend->>API: PATCH /posts/:id (scheduled_at)
  API->>DB: update POST (status=SCHEDULED, scheduled_at)
  Worker->>DB: pick scheduled posts (due)
  Worker->>API: fetch post details (or read DB)
  Worker->>XAPI: POST /create (with idempotency-key)
  XAPI-->>Worker: 200/201 (remote_post_id)
  Worker->>DB: update POST (status=SENT, sent_at, remote_post_id)
  alt XAPI failed
    Worker->>DB: update POST (status=FAILED, error)
    Worker->>RetrySvc: schedule retry
  end

  Note right of Worker: Idempotency keys prevent duplicates
```

Sequence diagram showing the lifecycle from draft → schedule → worker → post → success/failure.
